INT. CORPORATE TEAM-BUILDING ESCAPE ROOM - DAY

A fake dungeon with plywood walls painted to look like stone. A locked chest. A plastic skull on a pedestal. A digital clock on the wall counts down from 60:00. It reads 03:12.

Four coworkers are trapped in the room, every one of them wearing a lanyard. ARNOLD KOWALCZYK-ABARA (40s, rumpled shirt) kicks the chest. DESMOND PETROVA-OKAFOR (30s, red-faced, sweating) dumps a bag of plastic coins on the floor. PRUDENCE LINDQVIST-ADEYEMI (50s, reading glasses, a pen behind her ear) paces. NORMAN HOLLOWAY-LEE (30s, the intern) stares at the skull, hopeful.

He kicks the chest again. He shouts. He sits on it. He gets up and checks the other side, while he stares at the coins, then at him, and then at the clock.

ARNOLD
We're going to be late for the all-hands.

DESMOND
We're going to be dead, Arnold.

PRUDENCE
We're going to be fired.

NORMAN
Is it possible the skull is the key?

ARNOLD
It's plastic.

NORMAN
But keys can be plastic.

DESMOND
That's a skull, Norman!

Norman picks up the skull. Turns it over. Inside, taped to the cranium, a key. He holds it out. For a moment nobody breathes.

PRUDENCE
Well. Don't just stand there.

He fits it in the chest. The lid creaks open. Inside lies a laminated card: "CONGRATULATIONS! YOU HAVE ESCAPED. PLEASE RETURN YOUR LANYARDS."

The clock stops at 02:05.
